# Override Omarchy's default wifi-powersave udev rule.
#
# Omarchy's version keys on ATTR{type}=="Mains", ATTR{online}, which inherits
# the ROG Flow Z13's AC0.online flapping: while the battery is actively
# charging, AC0 flips 0 <-> 1 every 1-3 seconds, toggling Wi-Fi power save at
# the same rate (101 times in 14 minutes). That churn is a plausible
# contributor to the Wi-Fi instability documented in
# docs/wifi-investigation-2026-03-08.md.
#
# Matching ATTR{status}=="Discharging" here does not work either: the udev
# event fires before BAT0.status settles, so the rule can match the wrong
# branch. Instead this single rule fires a script that reads the settled status
# itself and applies the right mode.
#
# KERNEL=="BAT*" matches the kernel's system-battery names (BAT0, BAT1, ...) and
# excludes peripheral batteries such as the Elan touchpad's
# hid-0018:04F3:43C7.0008-battery-7.
#
# NOTE: No fixed --unit name — each udev event gets a unique auto-generated unit.
# A fixed name causes collisions when BAT0 emits several uevents for one
# transition (observed: two per replug), making every invocation after the first
# fail with "unit already exists".
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", KERNEL=="BAT*", ATTR{type}=="Battery", RUN+="/usr/bin/systemd-run --no-block --collect __HOME__/.local/bin/z13-wifi-powersave-auto"
